# Line endings: source, web, script and workflow files always use LF, on every system, so the tests and gofmt give the same result on Windows, macOS and Linux (Go's own tools expect LF).
*.go text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.css text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
go.mod text eol=lf
go.sum text eol=lf
# The licence files have no file extension, so they need their own lines: without them Windows checks them out with CRLF and the licence test fails there.
LICENSE text eol=lf
NOTICE text eol=lf
# Pictures and the built program are binary: never changed.
*.png binary
